  "visual": {
    "Well01": "Coherent composite inherits same separated thick roof boards and open pottery mouths, with baseline cask/support preserved.",
    "Well02": "Physical board separation and exposed thickness resolve prior planar roof. Softer coping construction is visible but restrained.",
    "Well03": "Real open blue throat and continuous pottery lips replace painted plugs and thin polygon edges. Compact interior UV eliminates folded radial streaks.",
    "Well04": "Same mouth improvements across actual vessel clusters; lying blue vessel now reads as open-neck pottery, retaining ground position and handles."
  },
  "limitations": [
    "Offline actual placement render proof, not live client or terrain collision proof.",
    "Outer pottery bodies and handles retain baseline coarse silhouette; this is a bounded mouth/throat remake.",
    "Smooth low-detail inside shading may look shallow at some views; depth and rim construction are visible in reverse/lying views.",
    "Well roof/coping change is restrained at reduced scale, stronger at normal view; no dramatic silhouette redesign claimed.",
    "Exact matching baseline zero-UV and nonpositive corner-normal exceptions retained, not repaired. Harmless baseline raw bone aliases were rotation-equivalent."
  ],
